Left over from k317 (2026-10-31): two oddities in `dzil build`, cause not yet known.
1. Every built file (89) has an empty `=head1 SUPPORT` section, which `podchecker` flags. It is probably the @Author::GETTY bundle's Pod::Weaver config, maybe tied to `no_cpan = 1` in dist.ini.
2. dzil prints `git: 'svn' is not a git command` during the build.

Done = for each one, say whether the cause is OCP's dist.ini/weaver.ini or the bundle (../p5-dist-zilla-pluginbundle-author-getty).
- If it's OCP: fix it here, and the next `dzil build` has neither.
- If it's the bundle: file a card on that repo's board (`karr --dir ../p5-dist-zilla-pluginbundle-author-getty create ... `, it lands in backlog), naming what OCP's build shows. Then close this one with a note naming the new card.

Lane: ocp-release-manager (release audit). Read-only on the bundle repo.

Cause: neither is OCP's dist.ini/weaver.ini. Both appear only in a build from a tree with no GitHub remote (git archive copy): the bundle then adds [Repository], which runs 'git svn info' (the svn noise), and the SUPPORT template has no bugtracker/IRC to render, leaving an empty =head1 SUPPORT. With origin git@github.com:Getty/kubernetes-ocp.git in .git/config a dzil build of HEAD 5935cc5 prints neither, SUPPORT has Issues, podchecker OK. Bundle-side wish filed as card 16 on the p5-dist-zilla-pluginbundle-author-getty board (backlog). No OCP change.
